<slide>
  theme: paper
  background: linear-gradient(160deg, #f4ecd8, #e8d9b5)
</slide>

<h2>Per-slide theme and background</h2>

<p>
  <c>theme: paper</c> and a CSS gradient background, for this slide only.
  The next slide goes back to the deck theme; the change crossfades.
</p>

<notes>
  Themes are sets of CSS variables, so a theme switch also recolors the code tokens.
</notes>
